- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests`

**How to implement.** Mapped points are validated against an experiment's scan and detector by one rule, and the load answers mapped points (001 §K 'Status badges: … validated (points) / … / out of range'; the S9.1 mapper's request: map multi-variable scans (`ScanAxis` / `ScanSetting`) instead of step 288's refusal; 001 §I: a dial-mounted item records raw readings, step 289). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`: the `<Compile>` lines of `ExperimentDataProxy.fs` and `ExperimentDataLoad.fs` move, in that order and with no comment, to directly after `ImportProfiles.fs` (step 300), so the data seam can speak mapped points; no Domain file compiled between their old and new places names them. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs`, after `MappedPoints`: (a) `ScanQuantity = { elementId : ElementId; label : ElementLabel; variable : VariableParameter; ranges : VariableRange list }`, one quantity a scan varies, with every range an axis gives it, and `member this.admits (value : SweptValue) : bool`, true when some range admits it (`MeasuredData.fs:admits`); (b) `type ExperimentScan with member this.quantities : ScanQuantity list`, the distinct `(elementId, variable)` pairs of `axes` (step 287) in order of first appearance, each with its first axis's label and the ranges of its axes in order, so A1's and A2's azimuth on one plate is one quantity (001 §Q AT-2); (c) `type MappedPoints with member this.validatedFor (detector : DetectorKind) (scan : ExperimentScan) : Result<MappedPoints, ExperimentDataError>`, the one validation of mapped points, answering the points unchanged or the first mismatch: `SeriesPoints` is step 288's rule, MOVED out of `loadAndValidate` with its texts, the validated series wrapped again; `CapturePoints` under an `Ellipsometer` is `DataUnitsMismatchErr` `the detector is an ellipsometer (records Ψ/Δ), but the data file is a Phone ROI CSV of intensities`, under a scan of no quantity passes (a dark line has nothing to range-check), under one quantity needs every row's `description.degrees` admitted, the first that is not being `DataRangeMismatchErr` `a description <x>° lies outside every range of <label> <variable.label>`, and under more quantities is `DataRangeMismatchErr` `a Phone ROI CSV holds one variable (its description), and the scan varies <n>`; `ObservationPoints` pass as read, each observation carrying its own configuration, which the study pairs with the experiment (S11.2); `ColumnPoints` with a `SignalReading` under an `Ellipsometer` is `DataUnitsMismatchErr` `the detector is an ellipsometer (records Ψ/Δ), but the mapping reads a signal`, rows whose scan cells do not number the quantities are `DataUnitsMismatchErr` `the import profile maps <k> scan column(s), and the scan varies <n>`, and the i-th cell of a row is the i-th quantity's: an angle unit (`spectralUnitOpt = None`) on a `VaryWaveLength` quantity, a spectral unit on any other, a `RawDialReading` on a quantity other than `VaryDialReading` and a `PhysicalScanValue` on a `VaryDialReading` one are each `DataUnitsMismatchErr` naming the column and the quantity, and a `displayValue` the quantity does not admit is `DataRangeMismatchErr` naming the value, the quantity's `unitLabel` and its label. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`: `loadAndValidate` (`ExperimentDataLoad.fs:loadAndValidate`, steps 261, 291) answers `Result<MappedPoints, ExperimentDataError>`: it reads as step 291 left it (the two built-in names through `tryLoadIntensity` and `tryLoadEllipsometric`, another name and a key selection refused with step 291's texts, reading nothing), wraps the series in `SeriesPoints` and answers its `validatedFor (detectorKindOf library slots) experiment.scan`; its own scan rule is deleted. `ExperimentDataBadge.ofCheck` (step 295) takes `(outcomeOpt : Result<MappedPoints, ExperimentDataError> option)`, `ValidatedDataBadge` holding the points' `pointCount`; nothing else in it changes. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: the one private validation function and the attach arm (steps 291, 295) pass the outcome to `ofCheck` as it comes. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs`: `validateExperiment` (`SolverHandoffView.fs:validateExperiment`) answers `HandoffReady points.pointCount`; its error arms are unchanged. Tests. `ImportProfileTests` (step 300) gains `a scan's quantities join the axes that vary one slot's variable`: over step 287's test-local `sample` slot, a scan whose first block varies `sample`'s R1 over 0…67.5° and whose second block varies `sample`'s R2 over 20…60° then R1 over 0…90° has two quantities, R1 with both ranges and then R2, and a dark line has none; and `mapped capture rows and column rows are validated against the experiment's scan and detector`: Phone ROI rows at 0° and 45° validate under a one-axis R1 scan over 0…360° and under a dark line, refuse a scan over 0…40° with `DataRangeMismatchErr` naming `45`, refuse the two-quantity scan above and an `Ellipsometer` detector; test-local `Lab scan` rows at 0° and 20° validate under that R1 scan, refuse a `VaryDialReading` scan (`DataUnitsMismatchErr`, a physical column on a dial), a `VaryWaveLength` scan (`DataUnitsMismatchErr`, an angle column on a wavelength) and the two-quantity scan (`DataUnitsMismatchErr`, one scan column for two quantities); and keyed observations pass under any scan. `ExperimentDataProxyTests`: `the data badge follows the attachment, its file's hash and its validation` (step 295) passes `Ok (SeriesPoints (IntensityData <the canned series>))` where it passed the series, its assertions kept, and `loading data validates a one-axis scan as before and refuses an X,Y file for a multi-variable scan` (step 288) and `loading data reads it through its import profile and refuses a profile or a row selection the X,Y files cannot serve` (step 291) expect `Ok (SeriesPoints _)` of the series they expected, every error assertion kept. `InverseConstructorTests` and `SolverHandoffWindowTests` pass as written.

**Acceptance.** After validation moves onto mapped points, `MappedPoints.validatedFor` MUST be the one rule checking an X,Y series as step 288 did, Phone ROI rows and mapped rows against the scan's quantities (units, raw dial vs physical, ranges) and the detector, with observations passing, and `loadAndValidate` and `ExperimentDataBadge.ofCheck` MUST carry mapped points; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a scan's quantities join the axes that vary one slot's variable` and `mapped capture rows and column rows are validated against the experiment's scan and detector`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `the data badge follows the attachment, its file's hash and its validation`, `loading data validates a one-axis scan as before and refuses an X,Y file for a multi-variable scan` and `loading data reads it through its import profile and refuses a profile or a row selection the X,Y files cannot serve`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.
